WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:03.036
-The president staged
a deranged

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:05.572
and deeply reckless photo op
when he left the hospital,

00:00:05.572 --> 00:00:08.707
despite still being symptomatic
with a highly infectious virus,

00:00:08.707 --> 00:00:11.377
and used it as an occasion
to tell Americans

00:00:11.377 --> 00:00:12.812
that COVID isn't a big deal.

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:14.647
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:18.751
♪♪

00:00:18.751 --> 00:00:21.253 line:0%
The president left Walter Reed
Medical Center yesterday,

00:00:21.253 --> 00:00:23.656 line:0%
making sure to gratuitously
touch the handrail

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:25.090 line:0%
a bunch of times
on his way down

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:26.492 line:0%
and, as he walked by reporters,

00:00:26.492 --> 00:00:28.027 line:0%
they asked him
a pointed question

00:00:28.027 --> 00:00:30.964 line:0%
that really sums up the state
of his presidency quite well.

00:00:30.964 --> 00:00:32.098 line:0%
[ Camera shutter clicking ]

00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:37.303
I know we do this a lot,
but imagine if, a year ago,

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:39.439
someone told you the president
would be asked,

00:00:39.439 --> 00:00:41.173
"Do you think you may be
a super spreader?"

00:00:41.173 --> 00:00:44.110
The only reaction is,
"What the [bleep] happened?"

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:46.546
It's like if I told you, a year
from now, someone would ask,

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:49.315
"Mr. President,
where did you put Montana?!"

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:51.550
I do feel like
the super spreader question's

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:53.386
not the one
you want to be getting

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:55.121
28 days before an election.

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:56.790
He's the president
and reporters are treating him

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:58.257
like he's the "Outbreak" monkey.

00:00:58.257 --> 00:01:00.192
"Mr. President, how many people
do you intend to bite?

00:01:00.192 --> 00:01:02.261
And a quick follow-up --
ankles or necks?"

00:01:02.261 --> 00:01:03.563
Gonna give
his next press conference

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:06.399
by popping out of the bushes
and hissing at reporters

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:08.634
before ducking away
to dodge a tranq dart.

00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:09.702
Did you get him, Curly?

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:11.470
"He's too fast!"

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:13.973
Usually, at the point in the
calendar, reporters are

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:15.675
asking the president questions
about the election.

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:18.411
In Trump's case, they're asking
him if he's Typhoid Larry.

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:20.079
"Mr. President,
if you win a second term,

00:01:20.079 --> 00:01:22.181
is there anyone else you'd
like to personally infect?"

00:01:22.181 --> 00:01:24.250
Of course, you got
to be careful with Trump

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:27.053
because he might think
super spreader is a compliment.

00:01:27.053 --> 00:01:29.021
[ As Trump ]
My Secret Service code name is
Spread Eagle.

00:01:29.021 --> 00:01:30.389
Y-Y-Yikes.

00:01:30.389 --> 00:01:33.359
Yikes, to that.
Can we cover that up?

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:35.261
Someone Photoshop
a ThighMaster in there.

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:37.430
There you go.
That's better.

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:40.499
It's not good,
but it's a little better.

00:01:40.499 --> 00:01:42.635
It's genuinely hard to recall
a moment in American life

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:44.170
that felt more unhinged

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:46.906
than the grotesque spectacle
we all witnessed last night --

00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:49.109
an infectious president
on powerful steroids

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:50.610
and experimental drugs
walking around

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:52.111
with a potentially deadly virus,

00:01:52.111 --> 00:01:53.680
making a big show
of leaving the hospital,

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:55.514
flying back
to the White House at sunset,

00:01:55.514 --> 00:01:57.516
and, just before
Joe Biden's town hall,

00:01:57.516 --> 00:01:59.219
taking his mask off
in front of the cameras

00:01:59.219 --> 00:02:01.921
and visibly gasping for air,

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:04.290
like he's been guarding
LeBron James all night.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:05.458
[ As Trump ]
[ Pants ]

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:08.160
I just, uh... [ Pants ]

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:10.763
gave 110%.

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:12.765
[ Pants ]

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:16.269
And I'm happy we held
LeBron to 38 point.

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:17.703
Looks like a "Solid Gold"
[ Laughing ] dancer

00:02:17.703 --> 00:02:20.707
trying to hold the tableaux
until the camera's off.

00:02:20.707 --> 00:02:24.010
[ Panting ]

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:25.712
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:28.748
Looks like he just got back
from a class at No SoulCycle.

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:31.384 line:0%
And, you know,
make sure to go to...

00:02:31.384 --> 00:02:34.721 line:0%
to vote for which one of those
three jokes you liked best.

00:02:34.721 --> 00:02:36.155
It's still active.

00:02:36.155 --> 00:02:37.723
You ever take a, you know,

00:02:37.723 --> 00:02:39.158
way too big a bong rip
in college

00:02:39.158 --> 00:02:40.392
and then,
you were too embarrassed,

00:02:40.392 --> 00:02:42.128
so you tried to hold it in
for as long as you could

00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:43.229
and then, you got so stoned,

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:44.397
you forgot
you were holding it in

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:45.397
and you somehow swallowed it?

00:02:45.397 --> 00:02:46.832
That's what he looks like.

00:02:46.832 --> 00:02:48.134
He either needs an oxygen mask

00:02:48.134 --> 00:02:49.768
or some peanut butter
and a bag of Funyuns.

00:02:49.768 --> 00:02:52.272
Seriously, was this stunt
supposed to convince us

00:02:52.272 --> 00:02:53.672
that COVID isn't a big deal?

00:02:53.672 --> 00:02:56.109
The only way this could've
been more of a cautionary tale

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:57.276
is if Trump started gnawing

00:02:57.276 --> 00:02:59.011
on a microphone,
thinking it was a drumstick.

00:02:59.011 --> 00:03:00.913
[ As Trump ]
See? I haven't lost
my sense of taste at all.

00:03:00.913 --> 00:03:03.582
Man, they're not kidding
about extra crispy, though.

00:03:03.582 --> 00:03:05.084
By the way, the only reason
we can even tell

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:06.286
that he was gasping for air

00:03:06.286 --> 00:03:08.588
was that the highly
infectious president,

00:03:08.588 --> 00:03:10.389
who is actively symptomatic

00:03:10.389 --> 00:03:12.158
with a potential deadly virus,

00:03:12.158 --> 00:03:13.559 line:0%
took his mask off

00:03:13.559 --> 00:03:15.562 line:0%
once he got back
to the White House.

00:03:15.562 --> 00:03:18.898
Wow. So the villain is unmasked
at the end of the episode.

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:21.234
The only thing missing
was Scooby and the gang.

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:22.835
-[ As Shaggy ]
Zoinks! It's Old Man Trump!

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:24.436
That was not good and I know it.

00:03:24.436 --> 00:03:25.571
[ As Trump ]
I would've gotten away
with it, too,

00:03:25.571 --> 00:03:27.239
if I just fired Velma
and replaced her

00:03:27.239 --> 00:03:28.908
with Kellyanne Conway.

00:03:28.908 --> 00:03:30.309
It's horrifying,
but I got to admit,

00:03:30.309 --> 00:03:33.012
it's also, you know,
just good movie making.

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:34.313
It's always
a dramatic high point

00:03:34.313 --> 00:03:35.815
when the villain
takes off his mask

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:38.351
so the innocent victim
can see their face.

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:40.219
The only thing missing
was the monologue

00:03:40.219 --> 00:03:41.888
about how long he's been
waiting for this.

00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:43.689
[ As Trump ]
Well, well...

00:03:43.689 --> 00:03:45.891
[ Breathes deeply ]

00:03:45.891 --> 00:03:47.460
...well.

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:48.594
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.594 --> 00:03:49.695
I just love how he took it off

00:03:49.695 --> 00:03:50.896
like it was a big reveal.

00:03:50.896 --> 00:03:54.133
We're familiar
with your face, my bro.

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:55.401
The only way that
would've been worth it

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:58.604
is if you were premiering
your new Selleck 'stache.

00:03:58.604 --> 00:04:00.440
And then, after that
insane spectacle,

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:03.443
Trump shot a taxpayer-funded
campaign-style ad

00:04:03.443 --> 00:04:05.544
with dramatic music,
as well as one of his weird

00:04:05.544 --> 00:04:07.780
straight-to-camera
Twitter videos where he rambled

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:10.249
about how his experience proves
COVID is not that big a deal.

00:04:10.249 --> 00:04:13.452
-I learned so much
about coronavirus

00:04:13.452 --> 00:04:15.354
and one thing that's
for certain --

00:04:15.354 --> 00:04:18.223
don't let it dominate you.

00:04:18.223 --> 00:04:20.359
Don't be afraid of it.

00:04:20.359 --> 00:04:21.360
You're gonna beat it.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:22.829
Don't let it dominate.

00:04:22.829 --> 00:04:25.030
Don't let it take
over your lives.

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:26.199
Don't let that happen.

00:04:26.199 --> 00:04:28.268
We have the greatest
country in the world.

00:04:28.268 --> 00:04:30.102
We're going back.
We're going back to work.

00:04:30.102 --> 00:04:31.337
We're gonna be out front.

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:33.539
And I know there's a risk,
there's a danger,

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:35.007
but that's okay.

00:04:35.007 --> 00:04:37.209
And, now, I'm better
and maybe I'm immune.

00:04:37.209 --> 00:04:38.444
I don't know.

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:39.979
[ As Trump ]
Maybe I'm an X-Man now.

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:41.179
Maybe I can fly.

00:04:41.179 --> 00:04:42.681
Maybe I have super speed!

00:04:42.681 --> 00:04:45.250
Like the Flash.
I don't know.

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:46.385
I tried to ask my doctors,

00:04:46.385 --> 00:04:47.719
but I couldn't hear them
over Judge Jeanine.

00:04:47.719 --> 00:04:49.688
We love the judge,
don't we, folks?

00:04:49.688 --> 00:04:51.290
The voice of an angel

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:53.259
that's been lit on fire.

00:04:53.259 --> 00:04:54.660
And what do you mean,
you don't know?

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:56.762
I thought you said you learned
so much about coronavirus.

00:04:56.762 --> 00:04:59.899
That seems like something
you'd want to look into first,

00:04:59.899 --> 00:05:02.467
especially since scientists
have been studying it for,

00:05:02.467 --> 00:05:04.236
I don't know, months now.
He sounds like a fifth grader

00:05:04.236 --> 00:05:06.539
bull[bleep] his way
through an oral report.

00:05:06.539 --> 00:05:08.641
"I learned so much
about the Louisiana Purchase,

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:10.910
yet, there are many answers
we will never know.

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:12.912
Was it the purchase of Louisiana

00:05:12.912 --> 00:05:16.048
or was it a purchase made
by someone named Louisiana?"

00:05:16.048 --> 00:05:18.017
Also, why does this video
look like a commercial

00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:19.518
for a reverse mortgage?

00:05:19.518 --> 00:05:20.919
If there was ever a commercial

00:05:20.919 --> 00:05:23.656
that needed the pharmaceutical
disclaimer, it's this one.

00:05:23.656 --> 00:05:27.026
[ Speaking rapidly ]

00:05:33.933 --> 00:05:35.201
Honestly, it's getting
hard to imagine

00:05:35.201 --> 00:05:36.702
new ways for him
to spread the virus.

00:05:36.702 --> 00:05:39.038
He's been holding rallies
and indoor events without masks

00:05:39.038 --> 00:05:41.207
or social distancing;
walking around near other people

00:05:41.207 --> 00:05:43.842
while he's infectious;
taking a sad,

00:05:43.842 --> 00:05:45.978
slow ride in his motorcade,
like a Pope

00:05:45.978 --> 00:05:47.180
who just got [bleep]canned

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:49.048
for stealing office supplies
from the Vatican.

00:05:49.048 --> 00:05:51.050
[ English accent ]
And there he goes,
Pope Donaldus,

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:52.952
sadly waving a goodbye.

00:05:52.952 --> 00:05:54.853
A fitting end for a pontiff

00:05:54.853 --> 00:05:57.022
who hid multiple
printer cartridges

00:05:57.022 --> 00:05:58.124
in his miter.

00:05:58.124 --> 00:05:59.858
And, now, he's back
to the White House

00:05:59.858 --> 00:06:01.961
and ditching his mask
while he's still contagious.

00:06:01.961 --> 00:06:04.163
He's exhaling a toxic virus,

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:06.131
like one of the Joker's
poison flowers...

00:06:06.131 --> 00:06:07.433
Nerd life!

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:09.001
...and, instead
of keeping his distance,

00:06:09.001 --> 00:06:10.970
he immediately gets rid
of the one thing

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:12.271
that could provide some level

00:06:12.271 --> 00:06:13.672
of protection
for the people around him,

00:06:13.672 --> 00:06:15.441
which isn't just
unsafe for them.

00:06:15.441 --> 00:06:17.209
It also sends an incredibly
dangerous signal

00:06:17.209 --> 00:06:18.243
to his supporters that,

00:06:18.243 --> 00:06:19.778
even if they might be
infectious,

00:06:19.778 --> 00:06:21.113
they don't need to wear a mask,

00:06:21.113 --> 00:06:23.282
a message he's been
sending for weeks

00:06:23.282 --> 00:06:24.684
by claiming, without evidence,

00:06:24.684 --> 00:06:26.985
that masks can have
negative effects

00:06:26.985 --> 00:06:28.754
and mocking Joe Biden
for wearing one.

00:06:28.754 --> 00:06:29.822
-There are a lot of people
who think

00:06:29.822 --> 00:06:31.257 line:0%
that masks are not good.

00:06:31.257 --> 00:06:32.625
I don't wear a mask like him.

00:06:32.625 --> 00:06:33.993
Every time you see him,
he's got a mask.

00:06:33.993 --> 00:06:36.596
He could be speaking
200 feet away from it

00:06:36.596 --> 00:06:38.998
and he shows up with the
biggest mask I've ever seen.

00:06:38.998 --> 00:06:40.766
Did you ever see a man
that likes a mask

00:06:40.766 --> 00:06:42.768
as much as him?
Because you know what?

00:06:42.768 --> 00:06:44.737
It gives him
a feeling of security.

00:06:44.737 --> 00:06:47.373
If I were a psychiatrist --

00:06:47.373 --> 00:06:48.841
[ Laughter and applause ]
Right?

00:06:48.841 --> 00:06:50.676
No, I'd say --
[ Cheering ]

00:06:50.676 --> 00:06:53.279
I'd say this guy's got
some big issues.

00:06:53.279 --> 00:06:54.747
-If you were a psychiatrist,

00:06:54.747 --> 00:06:56.849
your patients
would have to treat you.

00:06:56.849 --> 00:06:58.216
"I'm hearing voices, doc."

00:06:58.216 --> 00:06:59.818
[ As Trump ]
Me too. What would
you recommend?

00:06:59.818 --> 00:07:01.387
"I don't know.
Have you tried lithium?"

00:07:01.387 --> 00:07:03.756
I wonder how that mixes
with dexamethasone.

00:07:03.756 --> 00:07:04.857
That's my COVID medication.

00:07:04.857 --> 00:07:05.991
Did I mention I have COVID?

00:07:05.991 --> 00:07:07.326
You probably didn't hear me
through my mask.

00:07:07.326 --> 00:07:08.594
Oh, wait.
I'm not wearing one.

00:07:08.594 --> 00:07:09.796
Also, what do you mean,

00:07:09.796 --> 00:07:11.530
he's got the biggest mask
you've ever seen?

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:14.367
Could it just be that
your masks are the same size,

00:07:14.367 --> 00:07:15.802
but covers less of your face

00:07:15.802 --> 00:07:18.604
because your head is the size
of a waterlogged picnic ham?

00:07:18.604 --> 00:07:20.640
And what that is
is like it would happen

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:22.808
when there's a picnic
and it starts to rain, so,

00:07:22.808 --> 00:07:24.410
you know, everybody grabs
something, they run for cover,

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:25.778
but then, once you're
underneath an awning

00:07:25.778 --> 00:07:29.514
or whatever, someone says,
"Did anyone grab the ham?!"

00:07:29.514 --> 00:07:31.183
So it's a real thing.

00:07:31.183 --> 00:07:33.852
And even after Trump
was hospitalized with COVID

00:07:33.852 --> 00:07:36.422
and given a battery of powerful
and experimental drugs,

00:07:36.422 --> 00:07:39.324
his supporters are still
mocking Biden for wearing masks,

00:07:39.324 --> 00:07:40.793
like Rudy Giuliani,
who said this

00:07:40.793 --> 00:07:43.662
after a Fox anchor asked him
about Biden urging the president

00:07:43.662 --> 00:07:45.797
to listen to scientists
and support masks --

00:07:45.797 --> 00:07:48.767
-What would you say
to Joe Biden there?

00:07:48.767 --> 00:07:50.436 line:0%
-Well, I would say to Joe

00:07:50.436 --> 00:07:52.938 line:0%
that you don't really understand
what scientists are.

00:07:52.938 --> 00:07:55.208 line:0%
First of all, listen to your
doctors, that's for sure.

00:07:55.208 --> 00:07:56.842 line:0%
They know your personal history.

00:07:56.842 --> 00:07:58.810 line:0%
Doctors really
aren't scientists.

00:07:58.810 --> 00:08:00.412
-Do you think you know more
about scientists

00:08:00.412 --> 00:08:01.614
because you were created
by them?

00:08:01.614 --> 00:08:04.016
Rudy's just a bunch
of different body parts

00:08:04.016 --> 00:08:05.851
of deceased mobsters,
sewn together

00:08:05.851 --> 00:08:08.087
and shocked with electricity
until they came to life.

00:08:08.087 --> 00:08:09.788
[ European accent ]
Well, I couldn't find a neck,

00:08:09.788 --> 00:08:10.956
but maybe it'll work, anyway.

00:08:10.956 --> 00:08:12.925
Rise, my creation!

00:08:12.925 --> 00:08:15.327
Second, maybe your doctors
aren't really scientists,

00:08:15.327 --> 00:08:17.696
but then again,
I just assume your doctors work

00:08:17.696 --> 00:08:19.131
under the 59th Street Bridge.

00:08:19.131 --> 00:08:20.499
Doc, I got a rash.

00:08:20.499 --> 00:08:21.867
"Uh, you could try these pills.

00:08:21.867 --> 00:08:23.668
They fell off the back
of a truck."

00:08:23.668 --> 00:08:25.838
And then, there was Trump
campaign adviser Jason Miller,

00:08:25.838 --> 00:08:28.341
who criticized Biden
for making mask wearing

00:08:28.341 --> 00:08:29.942
such a big part of his campaign.

00:08:29.942 --> 00:08:31.977
-I'd say that,
with regard to Joe Biden,

00:08:31.977 --> 00:08:34.446 line:0%
I think, too often,
he's used the mask as a prop.

00:08:34.446 --> 00:08:35.981 line:0%
A mask is very important,

00:08:35.981 --> 00:08:37.315 line:0%
but even if he's --

00:08:37.315 --> 00:08:41.087 line:0%
He could be 20, 30 feet away
from the nearest person

00:08:41.087 --> 00:08:42.888 line:0%
and still have the mask on.

00:08:42.888 --> 00:08:45.457 line:0%
That's not gonna change
anything that's out there.

00:08:45.457 --> 00:08:47.926 line:0%
But also, we've seen,
with Joe Biden,

00:08:47.926 --> 00:08:50.495 line:0%
I mean, we can't all just stay
in our basement

00:08:50.495 --> 00:08:51.697 line:0%
for the rest of our lives.

00:08:51.697 --> 00:08:53.832 line:0%
We have to get out there
and live our lives

00:08:53.832 --> 00:08:56.068 line:0%
and take this on,
develop the vaccine,

00:08:56.068 --> 00:08:58.905 line:0%
develop more therapeutics,
and defeat it.

00:08:58.905 --> 00:09:00.238
-Alright, a couple of things.
First,

00:09:00.238 --> 00:09:02.007
what's up with your head, man?
You look like someone

00:09:02.007 --> 00:09:03.309
pumped too much air
into a football.

00:09:03.309 --> 00:09:05.711
Second, yes, he's trying
to model good behavior

00:09:05.711 --> 00:09:08.547
and lead by example,
by promoting mask wearing.

00:09:08.547 --> 00:09:09.782
Also, you work for Trump.

00:09:09.782 --> 00:09:11.317
You're the last person
who should accuse anyone

00:09:11.317 --> 00:09:12.317
of using a prop.

00:09:12.317 --> 00:09:13.552
Trump was literally caught

00:09:13.552 --> 00:09:15.721
signing a blank piece of paper
over the weekend,

00:09:15.721 --> 00:09:17.990
like a teenager practicing
his mom's signature

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:19.492
to get him out of gym class.

00:09:19.492 --> 00:09:20.525
[ As Trump ]
I'm as mad as you are, Coach,

00:09:20.525 --> 00:09:21.593
but you read the note.

00:09:21.593 --> 00:09:22.962
"And I'm sorry, Don.

00:09:22.962 --> 00:09:24.697
Your mother's name is Mom?"

00:09:24.697 --> 00:09:26.031
[ As Trump ]
Oh, no, I biffed it!

00:09:26.031 --> 00:09:29.468
And I love that that's
what they're still going with,

00:09:29.468 --> 00:09:31.537
the stupid basement line
for Biden,

00:09:31.537 --> 00:09:33.305 line:0%
despite the fact that,
in this clip from August,

00:09:33.305 --> 00:09:35.073 line:0%
he's biking more
than Donald Trump has biked,

00:09:35.073 --> 00:09:36.609 line:0%
I don't know, ever?

00:09:36.609 --> 00:09:38.744
I mean, that is possible, right?

00:09:38.744 --> 00:09:40.312
It's very hard to picture
Trump on a bike.

00:09:40.312 --> 00:09:43.515
Just the swinging
of the leg over the frame.

00:09:43.515 --> 00:09:45.184
Or the desiring of it.

00:09:45.184 --> 00:09:46.886
Just so hard
to picture Trump saying...

00:09:46.886 --> 00:09:49.087
[ As Trump ]
Should we take the bikes out?

00:09:49.087 --> 00:09:51.356
Nice day for a bike ride.

00:09:51.356 --> 00:09:53.392
Mel!

00:09:53.392 --> 00:09:55.527
[ Laughter ]
Mel!

00:09:55.527 --> 00:09:57.897
Should we take
the bikes out, Mel?!

00:09:57.897 --> 00:10:00.866
[ Laughter ]
I'm gonna go -- Mel!

00:10:00.866 --> 00:10:04.436
I'm gonna go check the tires,
make sure --

00:10:04.436 --> 00:10:07.006
Oh -- oh -- okay!

00:10:07.006 --> 00:10:08.240
[ Laughter ]

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:11.009
Alright.
Check your mail.

00:10:11.009 --> 00:10:12.778
[ Laughter ]
Let me love you, Mel!

00:10:12.778 --> 00:10:14.779
[ Laughter ]

00:10:14.779 --> 00:10:16.281
Yeah, whatever, sure.

00:10:16.281 --> 00:10:18.650
Biden's a basement troll.

00:10:18.650 --> 00:10:19.819
Go for it.

00:10:19.819 --> 00:10:21.020
And what do you mean,
we have to get out there

00:10:21.020 --> 00:10:22.521
and live our lives
and take this on?

00:10:22.521 --> 00:10:24.923
That makes no sense.
These people are so dumb.

00:10:24.923 --> 00:10:26.525 line:0%
They genuinely do not seem
to understand

00:10:26.525 --> 00:10:28.226 line:0%
the basics
of viral transmission.

00:10:28.226 --> 00:10:30.830 line:0%
For example,
conservative commentator
Hugh Hewitt tweeted...

00:10:43.074 --> 00:10:45.243
Well, I mean, that depends.
If Reagan was shot

00:10:45.243 --> 00:10:46.478
because he was juggling a bunch

00:10:46.478 --> 00:10:47.980
of loaded guns
in the Oval Office

00:10:47.980 --> 00:10:49.314
and one of them
accidentally went off,

00:10:49.314 --> 00:10:52.218
I feel like the applause
might've been a bit more muted.

00:10:52.218 --> 00:10:54.420
It's like...
[ Clapping] "This guy."

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:56.388
The president got the best
taxpayer-funded

00:10:56.388 --> 00:10:58.457
medical care in the world
and, instead of ensuring

00:10:58.457 --> 00:10:59.959
that every American
gets similar treatment,

00:10:59.959 --> 00:11:01.660
he's telling them to go out
and fight the virus

00:11:01.660 --> 00:11:03.062
because it's just not
that big a deal.

00:11:03.062 --> 00:11:05.464
He's proven, once again,
he has no regard

00:11:05.464 --> 00:11:07.232
for any life other than his own.

00:11:07.232 --> 00:11:09.768
He's recklessly putting
others in harm's way

00:11:09.768 --> 00:11:11.102
by holding
super spreading events,

00:11:11.102 --> 00:11:13.939
walking around without a mask
while he's infectious,

00:11:13.939 --> 00:11:15.441
and telling people
who don't have access

00:11:15.441 --> 00:11:17.343
to the same healthcare he has

00:11:17.343 --> 00:11:18.778
not to be afraid
of a deadly virus

00:11:18.778 --> 00:11:20.645
that's killed more than
200,000 Americans.

00:11:20.645 --> 00:11:22.547
And he's doing it all
to pump up his own ego.

00:11:22.547 --> 00:11:24.616
I'm no psychiatrist,
but I think it's safe to say...

00:11:24.616 --> 00:11:26.519
[ Cheering and applause ]
-This guy's got some big issues.

00:11:26.519 --> 00:11:28.220
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:32.090
♪♪

00:11:32.090 --> 00:11:33.592
God's Love We Deliver
cooks and brings

00:11:33.592 --> 00:11:35.027
